# .semgrepignore — paths excluded from Semgrep SAST scans.
#
# Semgrep reads this file (same syntax as .gitignore) and skips any path that
# matches. Exclude generated artifacts, vendored code, and directories that
# contain content we deliberately don't want flagged as application code
# (e.g. attached chat-log assets, compiled bundles, test fixture output).
#
# Keep this list conservative: only exclude paths that are either:
#   (a) not application code (generated, vendored, or uploaded content), or
#   (b) producing confirmed false-positives that have been triaged and
#       suppressed with inline `# nosemgrep` / `// nosemgrep` annotations
#       where the finding appears instead.

# ── Build output ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
dist/
server_dist/
.expo/

# ── Package manager caches / installed dependencies ─────────────────────────
node_modules/
web/node_modules/
.npm/

# ── Uploaded / pasted assets ─────────────────────────────────────────────────
# attached_assets/ contains copy-pasted chat logs, screenshots, and other
# non-code blobs. p/secrets rules flag credential-shaped strings inside these
# files — all of which are already known (and tracked in memory/MEMORY.md) as
# leaked test/reviewer credentials in historical chat pastes, not live secrets
# embedded in application code. Suppressing the whole directory keeps signal:
# noise high; the underlying credential rotation is tracked separately.
attached_assets/

# ── Database migrations (generated SQL / TypeScript) ─────────────────────────
drizzle/

# ── Minified / compiled third-party bundles ──────────────────────────────────
*.min.js
*.bundle.js

# ── Test fixture output / temporary files ────────────────────────────────────
tmp/
.cache/

# ── Expo / React Native generated files ──────────────────────────────────────
ios/
android/
